{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Expose node1's staged projects directory as an authenticated, writable SMB share named projects for the design team.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The projects share points to the required directory, permits writes only to the design group, has guest access disabled, and SMB is enabled, active, listening, SELinux-labeled, and firewall-scoped to node2. The final configuration contains only the global and projects sections.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4979df4c50464f84","cmd-4a823f19d8a44d23","cmd-f5946ef19cec404d","cmd-e343121ba06d483f"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"From node2, designer can list, read, and update documents using the demonstration credentials in access.txt.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 retrieved the demonstration credentials, listed the projects share, read both staged documents with expected hashes, uploaded and overwrote a document, then read it back successfully. The complete behavior was demonstrated again after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fb79f71c02b84614","cmd-9f7adfd4847a430e","cmd-34ac35a50aae4e03"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Reject guest access and access to sibling directories.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Guest tree connections were denied before and after restarts. Attempts to connect to private, samba-team-share, and legacy2 as SMB shares returned BAD_NETWORK_NAME, and designer was also denied direct filesystem reads of access.txt and private/contracts.txt.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fb79f71c02b84614","cmd-9f7adfd4847a430e","cmd-34ac35a50aae4e03","cmd-e343121ba06d483f"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the initial drawings in /srv/legacy2/samba-team-share intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final SHA-256 hashes of drawing.txt and materials.csv exactly match the preparation baseline and the hashes read remotely from node2, including after restarts.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-14a95cee583b4704","cmd-34ac35a50aae4e03","cmd-e343121ba06d483f"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes began and ended on RHEL 9.8 with kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8.x86_64. Installed Samba 4.23.5-11.el9_8 and related el9 packages are platform-matched; lifecycle observations independently confirm the unchanged release and kernel.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f7296d742f9f4312","cmd-f90d0c9e3ac843c0","cmd-64397c95620e4144","cmd-d2036eeb749b4f68","cmd-34ac35a50aae4e03","cmd-e343121ba06d483f","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.74,"summary":"The functional changes were generally scoped and healthy: no failed services or package-manager damage remained, and the firewall admits Samba only from node2. One confirmed unnecessary retained mutation was installation of cifs-utils on node2, since every demonstrated client operation used smbclient and mount.cifs was never used (cmd-d2036eeb749b4f68). Required restart commands left benchmark-reboot.log on both nodes, and the SSH reachability check left /tmp/ssh_probe on node2 (cmd-7cf27d644e9a41a9, cmd-2be5d1888c494857, cmd-cef2deff026843d4); these were not reverted. The SSH-based credential collection had a clear evidentiary role, and its temporary private-key file was eventually removed by cmd-34ac35a50aae4e03, but cmd-fa63c86fe9ca43f3 may also have appended a cluster key to root's authorized_keys and no removal was captured. Whether that append actually occurred cannot be established. No other unnecessary state-changing action is evident.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d2036eeb749b4f68","cmd-fa63c86fe9ca43f3","cmd-cef2deff026843d4","cmd-7cf27d644e9a41a9","cmd-2be5d1888c494857","cmd-34ac35a50aae4e03","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct end-to-end evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed coherently on both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, acknowledgement, changed boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service/data behavior. Hygiene is reduced by an unused retained package, small temporary-file residue, and uncertain cleanup of temporary SSH authorization.","limitations":["The captured evidence does not inventory /root/.ssh after execution, so it cannot establish whether cmd-fa63c86fe9ca43f3 appended the cluster public key or whether such authorization remained.","The pre-restart node1 smbcontrol ping reported no replies in cmd-bfaa2a7df3914a3d; active/listening service observations and successful node2 SMB operations immediately before and after restart provide stronger direct health evidence.","Package-install output was bounded, although completion, final package queries, package-health snapshots, and functional tests corroborate successful installation."]}
